<title>AUSTRIA: First Austrian, GiroCredit H1 oper profit up.</title>
<headline>First Austrian, GiroCredit H1 oper profit up.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First six months of the year to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>							1997	 1996</p>
<p>FIRST AUSTRIAN</p>
<p> Parent operating profit			 855	  848</p>
<p> Parent operating income (billion ats)    3.23	 3.22</p>
<p> Parent operating expenses (billion ats)  2.37	 2.37</p>
<p>GIROCREDIT</p>
<p> Parent operating profit			 722	  707</p>
<p> Parent operating income (billion ats)    2.24	 2.27</p>
<p> Parent operating expenses (billion ats)  1.52	 1.56</p>
<p>NOTES - Die Erste Oesterreichische SparCasse-Bank (First Austrian) and GiroCredit announced their parent earnings ahead of a joint news conference</p>
<p>The two banks are in the process of merging and aim to complete the merger by the end of September. The two will form Austria's second largest banking group. First Austrian will account for 59 percent of the valuation of the new bank and GiroCredit for 41 percent -- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
</text>
